---
description: Nebula shared work log — read before a task, append after
alwaysApply: true
---

This repo keeps a shared MEMORY LOG in three layers: `.claude/MEMORY.md` is the index (one line per
task — date, title, the TERMS and files it is about — newest first), `.claude/memory/gotchas.md` holds
the standing gotchas (the traps that outlive their task, one line each, grouped by TERM), and
`.claude/memory/entries/<date>-<slug>.md` hold each task's full Asked / Did / Gotchas.

**Before starting a task**, read `.claude/MEMORY.md` and `.claude/memory/gotchas.md` in full, then open
the entry files whose index line names the TERMS, crate, symptom or file the user is asking about
(`grep -ril '<symbol or TERM>' .claude/memory/entries` when the index is not enough). A recorded gotcha
is a mine already stepped on; a recorded decision is settled unless the user reopens it. Entries
describe what was true when written, so confirm any file or flag they name still exists before relying
on it.

**After finishing a task** that changed code or behavior, diagnosed a bug, or turned up something
non-obvious, read `.claude/skills/nebula-memory/SKILL.md` and follow it: one entry file, one index line,
and any durable trap into the standing gotchas. Skip it for pure questions and trivial edits — the log
is only useful if it stays free of restated diffs. Run `make memory-check` afterwards.
